  "worked_solution": "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{6} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=6$ and $r=3.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{6(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{2}(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & =3({3}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
